  "configuration_id": "config_026",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_019 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) at 0.542 accuracy, clearly establishing that avgpool aggregation and weighted fusion outperform transformer/concat for this multimodal setup. The remaining uncertainty is whether the specific RNA encoder (scgpt) is optimal for complementing the image features, or whether a different encoder like SCVI (a VAE-based latent representation) would interact more effectively with the imagenet_vit_l image features. Config_026 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) holds the three best-performing design choices (avgpool, weighted, imagenet_vit_l) constant while swapping the RNA encoder to SCVI, which captures a fundamentally different latent space (variational posterior) than scgpt (generative model). This is the most informative single-variable extension of the current best: if SCVI matches or exceeds scgpt, it opens a new direction; if it falls short, it confirms scgpt as the preferred RNA encoder and lets us focus remaining budget on other axes. With 5 experiments left, this targeted test maximizes information gain about the RNA encoder dimension without risking the already-validated aggregation/fusion/image-encoder choices."
}

